    "body": "## Summary\n\nAdds **ADR-037: CSS Value Functions — calc() / min() / max() / clamp()**. First spec-driven ADR after the arc's switch from \"fix what's broken on Wikipedia\" to \"implement missing CSS spec features.\"\n\n**Documentation only.** Implementation lands as a follow-up PR (3 commits: calc parser, var-inside-calc, docs).\n\n## The measurement\n\n### parse_length returns 0.0 for every calc form\n\n| Expression | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `calc(10px + 5px)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(2em + 8px)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(100% - 20px)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(10px * 2)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(100px / 4)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(calc(10px + 5px) * 2)` | **0.0** |\n| `calc(var(--x) + 4px)` | **0.0** |\n\nNot parsed at all.\n\n### Wikipedia's calc() usage\n\n- **162 occurrences**, **23 unique expressions**\n- **Operators**: `+` 79, `-` 62, `*` 15, `/` 1\n- **Units**: px 143, em/rem 107 each (from `var(--font-size-medium,1rem)` fallbacks), % 3, vh 1\n- **Properties**: background-size (23), mask-size (23), width (19), height (16), margin-right/left (4 each), padding-left/right (3/2), max-width/height (1 each), left/right (1 each)\n\n### First-viewport impact (5 elements at y<900)\n\n| Declaration | Currently | After fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `width: calc(var(--font-size-medium,1rem) + 4px)` | 2×2 | **20×20** |\n| `height: calc(...)` | 2×2 | **20×20** |\n| `padding-left: calc(8px + 8px + calc(...))` | 0 | **36px** |\n| `max-height: calc(100vh - (24px * 2))` × 2 | 0 | 0 (vh deferred, sticky deferred) |\n\n### The var()-inside-calc bug\n\nComputed value still shows raw `var(--font-size-medium,1rem)` inside `calc()`. **ADR-026 handles top-level `var()` but not `var()` nested inside `calc(...)`.**\n\nThat means even after shipping a calc parser, `calc(var(--x) + 4px)` would receive raw `var()` as an operand and return 0. **Fixing calc() without fixing var-inside-calc delivers zero visible delta.**\n\n## The decision\n\n**Bundle calc + var-inside-calc in one ADR.** Ship them together — calc() alone would be zero visible delta; the two features are coupled.\n\n### The math expression parser\n\nStandard recursive descent:\n\n```\nexpr    := term (('+' | '-') term)*\nterm    := factor (('*' | '/') factor)*\nfactor  := '-'? primary\nprimary := number unit? | '(' expr ')' | function '(' args ')'\n```\n\n- Nested parens + nested `calc()`\n- Unary negation (`calc(-1 * 12px)`)\n- Functions: `calc` (1-arg), `min` / `max` (n-ary), `clamp` (ternary)\n- Units: px, em, rem, %, pt (vh/vw deferred)\n\n### Unit resolution\n\n- `px + px`, `em + em` → add (same unit)\n- `% + px` → convert % to px via `parent_content_width`\n- `em + px` → convert em via `font_size`\n- `px * number`, `px / number` → scale\n- `px / px` → unitless\n\n### var()-inside-calc\n\nExtend ADR-026's cascade substitution to work inside the four math functions. Root cause of ADR-026's miss diagnosed in Commit 1's diagnostic.\n\n## Design decisions\n\n### Why bundle calc + var-inside-calc\n\nSplitting would mean shipping calc() with a documented \"no visible delta because var() unresolved\" caveat, then var-inside-calc separately with \"now visible delta.\" Two ADRs, one boolean of progress. Bundled, single ADR, single visible delta.\n\n### Why standard precedence\n\nCSS's `calc()` precedence matches standard math (`* /` before `+ -`). No CSS-specific oddity. Standard recursive descent is correct.\n\n### Why not vh/vw in v1\n\n`vh` requires `viewport_height` in `LengthContext`, which isn't threaded through layout today. Wikipedia uses `vh` once, in `max-height` on a sticky container. Sticky is deferred, so no visible delta from vh today.\n\n### ADR-027's narrow parser stays\n\n`parse_length_maybe_calc` in `stylesheet.cpp` handles only `calc(Npx ± Mpx)` for `@media` queries. Different evaluation context (no font-size at query time). Two callers, two behaviors, no forced coupling.\n\n## Deferred (ADR-038+)\n\n- `vh`, `vw`, `vmin`, `vmax`\n- Vertical % inside calc\n- `calc()` in grid-template / font-size\n- `attr()`, `counter()` (depend on pseudo-elements)\n- `round()`, `mod()`, `rem()` (CSS4 math functions)\n\n## Test plan\n\nImplementation will add ~18-20 tests in `[css][calc][adr-037]`:\n- All four operators + precedence\n- Nested parens + nested calc\n- Unary negation\n- `min` / `max` / `clamp` n-ary semantics\n- Unit conversions (em↔px, %↔px)\n- Non-calc controls (10px, 2em, auto)\n\nPlus 3+ var-inside-calc tests in `[css][var][adr-037]`.\n\n## Verification after implementation\n\n| Check | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| Search icon box | w=2 h=2 | **w=20 h=20** |\n| Search input left padding | 0 | **36px** |\n| First-viewport PNG diff | — | icon visible, text not colliding |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n\n- [ ] **Bundled scope accepted** — calc + var-inside-calc in one ADR (calc alone is zero delta)\n- [ ] **vh/vw deferral accepted** — 1 use in Wikipedia, sticky-deferred, zero first-viewport impact\n- [ ] **Vertical % deferral accepted** — no first-viewport usage\n- [ ] **ADR-027's narrow parser kept** — different evaluation context, no refactor\n- [ ] **var()-inside-calc bug** — root cause diagnosed in Commit 1, fix in Commit 2\n\nRefs #191\n",
